IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc23-hearing-procedure.l4 -- section 672.5 (Procedure at disposition hearing) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, subsections (1) to (15.3); (16) is repealed.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively), from the text alone. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation
-- (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Form: see the header of ccc23-assessment.l4. Seams taken as inputs (PLAN.md section 6, ccc23 row): `s 2 victim: the purpose is section 672.5` and
-- `s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)`, both MAYBE BOOLEAN; a NOTHING from either is carried through, never turned into FALSE.

§ `Section 672.5(1) to (5.2) -- The section governs; the parties; notice`

-- 672.5(1): a hearing held by a court or Review Board to make or review a disposition in respect of an accused, including a hearing referred to in subsection 672.84(1) or (3), shall be held in accordance with this section.
-- src:13566 | 672.5 (1) A hearing held by a court or Review Board to make or review a disposition in respect of an accused, including a hearing referred to in subsection 672.84(1) or (3), shall be held in accordance with this section.
@ref s 672.5(1) (src:13566)
GIVEN `it is a hearing held by a court or Review Board to make or review a disposition in respect of an accused, including a hearing referred to in subsection 672.84(1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.5(1) the hearing is to be held in accordance with section 672.5` MEANS
    IF `it is a hearing held by a court or Review Board to make or review a disposition in respect of an accused, including a hearing referred to in subsection 672.84(1) or (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A hearing held by a court or Review Board to make or review a disposition in respect of an accused"

-- 672.5(2): the hearing may be conducted in as informal a manner as is appropriate in the circumstances.
-- src:13568 | (2) The hearing may be conducted in as informal a manner as is appropriate in the circumstances.
@ref s 672.5(2) (src:13568)
GIVEN `the informal manner is appropriate in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.5(2) the hearing may be conducted informally` MEANS
    IF `the informal manner is appropriate in the circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as informal a manner as is appropriate in the circumstances"

-- 672.5(3): on application, the court or Review Board shall designate as a party the Attorney General of the province where the disposition is to be made and, where an accused is transferred from another province, the Attorney General of the province from which the accused is transferred.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13570 | (3) On application, the court or Review Board shall designate as a party the Attorney General of the province where the disposition is to be made and, where an accused is transferred from another province, the Attorney General of the province from which the accused is transferred.
@ref s 672.5(3) (src:13570)
GIVEN `an application is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General is the Attorney General of the province where the disposition is to be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is transferred from another province and the Attorney General is the Attorney General of the province from which the accused is transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.5(3) the court or Review Board must designate the Attorney General as a party` MEANS
    IF `an application is made` AND (`the Attorney General is the Attorney General of the province where the disposition is to be made` OR `the accused is transferred from another province and the Attorney General is the Attorney General of the province from which the accused is transferred`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On application, the court or Review Board shall designate as a party the Attorney General"

-- 672.5(4): the court or Review Board may designate as a party any person who has a substantial interest in protecting the interests of the accused, if the court or Review Board is of the opinion that it is just to do so.
