§ `Section 672.5(6) to (13.04) -- Public, counsel, presence, evidence, remote appearance`

-- 672.5(6): where the court or Review Board considers it to be in the best interests of the accused and not contrary to the public interest, the court or Review Board may order the public or any members of the public to be excluded from the hearing or any part of the hearing.
-- fork: F-GRANT-WHERE
-- src:13580 | (6) Where the court or Review Board considers it to be in the best interests of the accused and not contrary to the public interest, the court or Review Board may order the public or any members of the public to be excluded from the hearing or any part of the hearing.
@ref s 672.5(6) (src:13580)
GIVEN `the court or Review Board considers it to be in the best interests of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court or Review Board considers it not contrary to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.5(6) the court or Review Board may order the public to be excluded from the hearing` MEANS
    IF `the court or Review Board considers it to be in the best interests of the accused` AND `the court or Review Board considers it not contrary to the public interest`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the court or Review Board considers it to be in the best interests of the accused and not contrary to the public interest"

