    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The accused or any other party has the right to be represented by counsel"

-- 672.5(8): if an accused is not represented by counsel, the court or Review Board shall, either before or at the time of the hearing, assign counsel to act for any accused (a) who has been found unfit to stand trial; or (b) wherever the interests of justice so require.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13584 | (8) If an accused is not represented by counsel, the court or Review Board shall, either before or at the time of the hearing, assign counsel to act for any accused
-- src:13585 | (a) who has been found unfit to stand trial; or
-- src:13586 | (b) wherever the interests of justice so require.
@ref s 672.5(8); s 672.5(8)(a); s 672.5(8)(b) (src:13584-13586)
GIVEN `the accused is represented by counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has been found unfit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `the interests of justice so require` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.5(8) the court or Review Board must assign counsel to act for the accused` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the accused is represented by counsel`) AND (`the accused has been found unfit to stand trial` OR `the interests of justice so require`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an accused is not represented by counsel, the court or Review Board shall, either before or at the time of the hearing, assign counsel to act for any accused"

-- 672.5(8.1): where counsel is assigned pursuant to subsection (8) and legal aid is not granted to the accused pursuant to a provincial legal aid program, the fees and disbursements of counsel shall be paid by the Attorney General to the extent that the accused is unable to pay them.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13588 | (8.1) Where counsel is assigned pursuant to subsection (8) and legal aid is not granted to the accused pursuant to a provincial legal aid program, the fees and disbursements of counsel shall be paid by the Attorney General to the extent that the accused is unable to pay them.
@ref s 672.5(8.1) (src:13588)
GIVEN `counsel is assigned pursuant to subsection 672.5(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `legal aid is granted to the accused pursuant to a provincial legal aid program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.5(8.1) the Attorney General must pay the fees and disbursements of counsel` MEANS
    IF `counsel is assigned pursuant to subsection 672.5(8)` AND NOT `legal aid is granted to the accused pursuant to a provincial legal aid program`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where counsel is assigned pursuant to subsection (8) and legal aid is not granted to the accused pursuant to a provincial legal aid program"

@ref s 672.5(8.1) (src:13588)
GIVEN `the fees and disbursements of counsel, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount that the accused is able to pay, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the Attorney General must pay, by s 672.5(8.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 672.5(8.1) the amount the Attorney General must pay, in dollars` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Attorney General must pay, by s 672.5(8.1)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST (IF `the fees and disbursements of counsel, in dollars` MINUS `the amount that the accused is able to pay, in dollars` AT LEAST 0 THEN `the fees and disbursements of counsel, in dollars` MINUS `the amount that the accused is able to pay, in dollars` ELSE 0)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states no payment where it does not apply
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of subsection 672.5(8.1) is carried through

-- 672.5(8.2): where counsel and the Attorney General cannot agree on the fees or disbursements of counsel, the Attorney General or the counsel may apply to the registrar of the court and the registrar may tax the disputed fees and disbursements.
