GIVEN `the court or chairperson considers the conditions proper` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.5(10)(a) the court or chairperson may permit the accused to be absent from the hearing` MEANS
    IF `the court or chairperson considers the conditions proper`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on such conditions as the court or chairperson considers proper"

-- fork: F-GRANT-WHERE
@ref s 672.5(10)(b); s 672.5(10)(b)(i); s 672.5(10)(b)(ii); s 672.5(10)(b)(iii) (src:13596-13599)
GIVEN `the accused interrupts the hearing so that to continue in the presence of the accused would not be feasible` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (i)
      `the court or chairperson is satisfied that failure to do so would likely endanger the life or safety of another person or would seriously impair the treatment or recovery of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (ii)
      `it is in order to hear, in the absence of the accused, evidence, oral or written submissions, or the cross-examination of any witness concerning whether grounds exist for removing the accused pursuant to subparagraph (ii)` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (iii)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.5(10)(b) the court or chairperson may cause the accused to be removed and barred from re-entry` MEANS
    IF `the accused interrupts the hearing so that to continue in the presence of the accused would not be feasible` OR `the court or chairperson is satisfied that failure to do so would likely endanger the life or safety of another person or would seriously impair the treatment or recovery of the accused` OR `it is in order to hear, in the absence of the accused, evidence, oral or written submissions, or the cross-examination of any witness concerning whether grounds exist for removing the accused pursuant to subparagraph (ii)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "cause the accused to be removed and barred from re-entry for the whole or any part of the hearing (i) where the accused interrupts the hearing"

-- 672.5(9): subject to subsection (10), the accused has the right to be present during the whole of the hearing. The two inputs are the answers of paragraphs (10)(a) and (10)(b): when either lets the accused be absent or removed, subsection (9) yields (NOTHING).
-- fork: F-ENTITLED, F-SUBJECT
-- src:13592 | (9) Subject to subsection (10), the accused has the right to be present during the whole of the hearing.
@ref s 672.5(9) (src:13592)
