-- 672.5(13.03): when deciding whether to make an order under (13.01), the court or Review Board must take into account (a) the accused's right to a review of their disposition; (b) the location and personal circumstances of the accused, including any potential adverse effects on the accused's mental condition;
-- (c) the suitability of the available technology and the location; (d) the accused's opportunity to communicate privately with legal counsel or to have access to legal advice; (e) the subject matter and the anticipated complexity of the hearing; and (f) any other factor that the court or Review Board considers relevant.
-- src:13613 | (13.03) When deciding whether to make an order under subsection (13.01), the court or Review Board must take into account the following factors:
-- src:13614 | (a) the accused’s right to a review of their disposition;
-- src:13615 | (b) the location and personal circumstances of the accused, including any potential adverse effects of an audioconference or videoconference on the accused’s mental condition;
-- src:13616 | (c) the suitability of the available technology and the location from where the parties will participate in the hearing;
-- src:13617 | (d) the accused’s opportunity to communicate privately with legal counsel, if they are represented, or to have access to legal advice during the hearing;
-- src:13618 | (e) the subject matter and the anticipated complexity of the hearing; and
-- src:13619 | (f) any other factor that the court or Review Board considers relevant.
@ref s 672.5(13.03); s 672.5(13.03)(a); s 672.5(13.03)(b); s 672.5(13.03)(c); s 672.5(13.03)(d); s 672.5(13.03)(e); s 672.5(13.03)(f) (src:13613-13619)
GIVEN `the court or Review Board is deciding whether to make an order under subsection 672.5(13.01)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the accused’s right to a review of their disposition` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `it is the location and personal circumstances of the accused, including any potential adverse effects of an audioconference or videoconference on the accused’s mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
      `it is the suitability of the available technology and the location from where the parties will participate in the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
      `it is the accused’s opportunity to communicate privately with legal counsel, if they are represented, or to have access to legal advice during the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)
      `it is the subject matter and the anticipated complexity of the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (e)
      `it is any other factor that the court or Review Board considers relevant` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (f)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.5(13.03) the court or Review Board must take the factor into account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court or Review Board is deciding whether to make an order under subsection 672.5(13.01)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When deciding whether to make an order under subsection (13.01)"
        IF `it is the accused’s right to a review of their disposition` OR `it is the location and personal circumstances of the accused, including any potential adverse effects of an audioconference or videoconference on the accused’s mental condition` OR `it is the suitability of the available technology and the location from where the parties will participate in the hearing` OR `it is the accused’s opportunity to communicate privately with legal counsel, if they are represented, or to have access to legal advice during the hearing` OR `it is the subject matter and the anticipated complexity of the hearing` OR `it is any other factor that the court or Review Board considers relevant` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a factor that the court or Review Board does not consider relevant is not named

-- 672.5(13.04): if the court or Review Board decides to make the order, it must provide reasons in writing.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13621 | (13.04) If the court or Review Board decides to make the order, it must provide reasons in writing.
