§ `Section 672.5(13.1) to (15.3) -- Adjournment, victims`

-- 672.5(13.1): the Review Board may adjourn the hearing for a period not exceeding thirty days if necessary for the purpose of ensuring that relevant information is available to permit it to make or review a disposition or for any other sufficient reason.
-- fork: F-GRANT-IF, F-CAP
-- src:13623 | (13.1) The Review Board may adjourn the hearing for a period not exceeding thirty days if necessary for the purpose of ensuring that relevant information is available to permit it to make or review a disposition or for any other sufficient reason.
@ref s 672.5(13.1) (src:13623)
GIVEN `the adjournment is necessary for the purpose of ensuring that relevant information is available to permit the Review Board to make or review a disposition, or for any other sufficient reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days of the adjournment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.5(13.1) the Review Board may adjourn the hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the days of the adjournment` GREATER THAN 30 THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period not exceeding thirty days"
        IF `the adjournment is necessary for the purpose of ensuring that relevant information is available to permit the Review Board to make or review a disposition, or for any other sufficient reason` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if necessary for the purpose of ensuring that relevant information is available to permit it to make or review a disposition or for any other sufficient reason"

-- 672.5(13.2): on receiving an assessment report, the court or Review Board shall determine whether, since the last time the disposition was made or reviewed, there has been any change in the mental condition of the accused that may provide grounds for the discharge of the accused
-- under paragraph 672.54(a) or (b) and, if there has been such a change, the court or Review Board shall notify every victim of the offence that they are entitled to file a statement in accordance with subsection (14).
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13625 | (13.2) On receiving an assessment report, the court or Review Board shall determine whether, since the last time the disposition in respect of the accused was made or reviewed there has been any change in the mental condition of the accused that may provide grounds for the discharge of the accused under paragraph 672.54(a) or (b) and, if there has been such a change, the court or Review Board shall notify every victim of the offence that they are entitled to file a statement in accordance with subsection (14).
@ref s 672.5(13.2) (src:13625)
GIVEN `the court or Review Board receives an assessment report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been a change in the mental condition of the accused that may provide grounds for the discharge of the accused under paragraph 672.54(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.5(13.2) the court or Review Board must notify every victim that they are entitled to file a statement` MEANS
    IF `the court or Review Board receives an assessment report` AND `there has been a change in the mental condition of the accused that may provide grounds for the discharge of the accused under paragraph 672.54(a) or (b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if there has been such a change, the court or Review Board shall notify every victim of the offence"

@ref s 672.5(13.2) (src:13625)
GIVEN `the court or Review Board receives an assessment report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.5(13.2) the court or Review Board must determine whether there has been a change in the mental condition of the accused` MEANS
    IF `the court or Review Board receives an assessment report`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On receiving an assessment report"

-- 672.5(13.3): if the Review Board refers to the court for review under subsection 672.84(1) a finding that an accused is a high-risk accused, it shall notify every victim of the offence that they are entitled to file a statement with the court in accordance with subsection (14).
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13627 | (13.3) If the Review Board refers to the court for review under subsection 672.84(1) a finding that an accused is a high-risk accused, it shall notify every victim of the offence that they are entitled to file a statement with the court in accordance with subsection (14).
@ref s 672.5(13.3) (src:13627)
