    IF `the Review Board refers to the court for review under subsection 672.84(1) a finding that an accused is a high-risk accused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Review Board refers to the court for review under subsection 672.84(1) a finding that an accused is a high-risk accused"

-- 672.5(14): a victim of the offence may prepare and file with the court or Review Board a written statement describing the physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss suffered by the victim as the result of the commission of the offence and the impact of the offence on the victim.
-- Form 48.2 in Part XXVIII, or a form approved by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the court or Review Board is exercising its jurisdiction, must be used for this purpose. The victim is the answer of s 2 "victim" (extended for this section) or of s 2.2 (a person acting for a dead or incapable victim).
-- fork: F-MUST-BARE
-- src:13629 | (14) A victim of the offence may prepare and file with the court or Review Board a written statement describing the physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss suffered by the victim as the result of the commission of the offence and the impact of the offence on the victim. Form 48.2 in Part XXVIII, or a form approved by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the court or Review Board is exercising its jurisdiction, must be used for this purpose.
@ref s 672.5(14) (src:13629)
GIVEN `the person is a victim of the offence, by s 2 victim: the purpose is section 672.5` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, by s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the statement is in Form 48.2, or in a form approved by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the court or Review Board is exercising its jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.5(14) the victim may prepare and file a written statement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is a victim of the offence, by s 2 victim: the purpose is section 672.5` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, by s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A victim of the offence may prepare and file" (a person who is not a victim, or whose standing as a victim is itself not covered, is not covered)
        IF `the statement is in Form 48.2, or in a form approved by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the court or Review Board is exercising its jurisdiction` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Form 48.2 in Part XXVIII, or a form approved by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the court or Review Board is exercising its jurisdiction, must be used for this purpose"

-- 672.5(15): the court or Review Board shall ensure that a copy of any statement filed in accordance with subsection (14) is provided to the accused or counsel for the accused, and the prosecutor, as soon as practicable after a verdict of NCR is rendered in respect of the offence.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13631 | (15) The court or Review Board shall ensure that a copy of any statement filed in accordance with subsection (14) is provided to the accused or counsel for the accused, and the prosecutor, as soon as practicable after a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered in respect of the offence.
