    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a copy of any statement filed in accordance with subsection (14)"

-- 672.5(15.1): the court or Review Board shall, at the request of a victim, permit the victim to read a statement prepared and filed in accordance with subsection (14), or to present the statement in any other manner that the court or Review Board considers appropriate,
-- unless the court or Review Board is of the opinion that the reading or presentation of the statement would interfere with the proper administration of justice.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13633 | (15.1) The court or Review Board shall, at the request of a victim, permit the victim to read a statement prepared and filed in accordance with subsection (14), or to present the statement in any other manner that the court or Review Board considers appropriate, unless the court or Review Board is of the opinion that the reading or presentation of the statement would interfere with the proper administration of justice.
@ref s 672.5(15.1) (src:13633)
GIVEN `a victim requests to read or present a statement prepared and filed in accordance with subsection 672.5(14)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court or Review Board is of the opinion that the reading or presentation of the statement would interfere with the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.5(15.1) the court or Review Board must permit the victim to read or present the statement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a victim requests to read or present a statement prepared and filed in accordance with subsection 672.5(14)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at the request of a victim"
        IF `the court or Review Board is of the opinion that the reading or presentation of the statement would interfere with the proper administration of justice` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the court or Review Board is of the opinion that the reading or presentation of the statement would interfere with the proper administration of justice"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 672.5(15.2): the court or Review Board shall, as soon as practicable after a verdict of NCR is rendered in respect of an offence and before making a disposition under section 672.45, 672.47 or 672.64, inquire of the prosecutor or a victim of the offence, or any person representing a victim,
-- whether the victim has been advised of the opportunity to prepare a statement referred to in subsection (14).
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13635 | (15.2) The court or Review Board shall, as soon as practicable after a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered in respect of an offence and before making a disposition under section 672.45, 672.47 or 672.64, inquire of the prosecutor or a victim of the offence, or any person representing a victim of the offence, whether the victim has been advised of the opportunity to prepare a statement referred to in subsection (14).
@ref s 672.5(15.2) (src:13635)
GIVEN `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered in respect of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court or Review Board has not yet made a disposition under section 672.45, 672.47 or 672.64` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.5(15.2) the court or Review Board must inquire whether the victim has been advised of the opportunity to prepare a statement` MEANS
    IF `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered in respect of the offence` AND `the court or Review Board has not yet made a disposition under section 672.45, 672.47 or 672.64`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered in respect of an offence and before making a disposition under section 672.45, 672.47 or 672.64"

-- 672.5(15.3): on application of the prosecutor or a victim or of its own motion, the court or Review Board may adjourn the hearing held under section 672.45, 672.47 or 672.64 to permit the victim to prepare a statement referred to in subsection (14)
-- if the court or Review Board is satisfied that the adjournment would not interfere with the proper administration of justice.
